{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id518127197"}, "name":{"label":"Bridgmen"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-09T23:23:57-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.97"}, "id":{"label":"14532000822"}, "title":{"label":"You get 2"}, "content":{"label":"My previous allowed lyrics are now flagged as inappropriate content. This is NOT free expression in Music. Nothing foul aside from some swear words and metaphors. We are talking about Music here, a medium that should be expressed as freely as Art. You should only flag when trying to share within the application. NOT during creation or Download. The lyric edit is wonky and unpredictable at best. Do you like the vocal tone, speed and read you got? too bad, it will change. You might even bounce genders in singers. That is not a system that should be available in the app then. Let alone have people purchase. It is faulty. There's more work to do. You guys had a nice thing going and it has gone down hill with these changes. Very Sad indeed.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6482289804&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
